    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d783-a1">

                <pb facs="0738" n="640" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg640"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Romanos to Mr.
                            Hardy.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-03-18"><hi rendition="#italic">March 18</hi> (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">G. S</hi>.), <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I hastened to transmit your note
                    of February 20 to my colleague of the department of war.</p>
                <p>Mr. Tsamados informs me that he deeply regrets that he can not release L.
                    Economopoulos from military service.</p>
                <p>In fact, Mr. Minister, the soldier in question, before acquiring American
                    citizenship, should have obtained permission to abandon his Greek nationality
                    according to the forms required by our civil code and discharged his military
                    obligations to the country of his birth.</p>
                <p>I take this occasion to renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Romanos.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
